DINOv3 ConvNeXt-L backbone + same transformer head as dino/train_dino_transformer.py
- backbone starts from DINOv3 LVD-1689M weights (no DinoClassifier stage), trained end-to-end on video bags
- adapter turns the 1536x16x16 feature map (512px input) into one 1024-d vector per frame:
  linear_attnpool (1x1 conv + LN + 2D sin/cos PE + learnable-query attention pooling, default) or linear_mean
- no temporal encoding, no attention entropy loss
- defaults = best unfrozen hp sweep config (8 heads, 1 block, lr 5e-5, backbone_lr_mult 0.3, distance_scale 0.2), but 12 epochs / lr_step 6 (generic, not DR-tuned, backbone needs longer than the ViT runs)
- final LayerNorm after the transformer blocks (proper pre-norm stack, unlike dino/train_dino_transformer.py)
- gradient accumulation was tried and removed (one optimizer step per video, shared transformer.utils.train_one_epoch_trans)
- Paxos2025 only: job script uses mil_{train,val}_2025.json, no --fused_dataset

2026-10-13 collapse diagnosis
- first runs (raw features, accum 4, lr 5e-5; frozen lr 3e-4) predicted one grade for all val videos every epoch (QWK 0)
- generic ConvNeXt features: cos sim between videos ~0.94 (one shared direction), but a standardized logistic-regression probe on GAP features gets val QWK ~0.78
- fix: per-channel standardization of the feature map with train-set stats (feat_mean/feat_std buffers)
- head-only tests on cached frozen features: lr 3e-4 always collapses (even with grad clipping), lr 1e-4 seed-dependent (0.56-0.77), lr 5e-5/3e-5 standardized stable (~0.80-0.82); distance scaling no clear effect; linear_mean ~ linear_attnpool
- warmup (backbone frozen 3 epochs, then x0.3 = 1.5e-5): QWK 0.64 -> 0.000 within the first unfrozen epoch, train loss back to start level; never recovered. Unfreezing itself breaks the features, not the random head. --freeze_epochs removed again.
- frozen backbone, standardized, lr 5e-5 (full run, 8 epochs): best val QWK 0.758 (epoch 5), final 0.704
- warmup (backbone frozen 3 epochs, then x0.3 = 1.5e-5): QWK 0.64 -> 0.000 within the first unfrozen epoch, train loss back to start level; never recovered. Unfreezing itself breaks the features, not the random head. --freeze_epochs removed again.
- frozen backbone, standardized, lr 5e-5 (full run, 8 epochs): best val QWK 0.758 (epoch 5), final 0.704
- unfreeze diagnostic (from best frozen ckpt, head 5e-5 / backbone 1.5e-5 Adam, logs convnext/logs/unfreeze_diag_*.log):
  within 50 steps (backbone weights changed only ~0.2%) the raw backbone features drift by ~2x their own norm and
  all videos map to the same adapter vector (cos sim 0.66 -> 1.00), probe preds one grade. Same with std clamped
  at its median, with layer-scale gammas frozen, and in fp32 -> not standardization, not gamma, not fp16.
  feat_std range is only 0.35-3.0 (median 0.76), no tiny-std channels.
- LR schedule switched from StepLR (--lr_step) to per-epoch cosine annealing down to --min_lr (default 1e-7), applied to both head and backbone groups

2026-10-14 linear_mean, backbone unfrozen x0.1 (first unfrozen runs that didn't collapse), Paxos2025 split_1 (same videos as stratified_splits_paxos2025/split_1):
- std on, lr 5e-5, 12 ep StepLR(6):          best QWK 0.864 (ep 10), ref recall 0.788; last 0.859
- std off, lr 5e-5, 12 ep StepLR(6):         best QWK 0.830 (ep 11), ref recall 0.848; QWK 0 for epochs 0-4, then recovered
- std off, lr 1e-5, 18 ep cosine to 1e-7:    best QWK 0.848 (ep 15), ref recall 0.818; last 0.840; smoother, no collapse phase
- standardization is not strictly required: it gives a faster/more stable start, but unstandardized runs recover
- --cluster_sample added (same as dino/train_dino_transformer.py: train = random member per k-means cluster, val = medoids; Paxos2025 only)

2026-10-14 linear_mean, unfrozen backbone x0.1 (all Paxos2025 split_1, same 60 val videos as the ViT baseline):
- standardized, lr 5e-5, StepLR@6, 12 ep: best QWK 0.864 (ep 10, ref recall 0.788), final 0.859  <- best ConvNeXt so far
- no standardization, lr 5e-5, StepLR@6, 12 ep: one grade for ep 0-4, then recovers; best 0.830 (ep 11, ref recall 0.848)
- no standardization, lr 1e-5, cosine to 1e-7, 18 ep: learns from ep 1; best 0.848 (ep 15, ref recall 0.818), ep 12-17 stable 0.82-0.85
